.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_PROBE_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_probe_new ,
.Nm dtfl_probe_free ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_probe_with ,
.Nm dtfl_probe_less_than ,
.Nm dtfl_probe_less_equal ,
.Nm dtfl_probe_done ,
.Nm dtfl_probe_frontier
.Nd monitor progress at a stream
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_probe *
.Fn dtfl_probe_new "void"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_probe_free "dtfl_probe *p"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_probe_with "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_probe *p"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_probe_less_than "const dtfl_probe *p" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_probe_less_equal "const dtfl_probe *p" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_probe_done "const dtfl_probe *p"
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_probe_frontier "const dtfl_probe *p" "size_t *n"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A probe reports which timestamps have elapsed at a point in a dataflow.
.Fn dtfl_probe_new
allocates one.
.Fn dtfl_stream_probe_with
inserts a pass-through operator in
.Fa st
that mirrors the stream's frontier into
.Fa p
and returns the stream unchanged, so the probe can be attached without
otherwise altering the computation.
A probe observes one stream's class.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_probe_less_than
returns true while the frontier is strictly before
.Fa t ,
and
.Fn dtfl_probe_less_equal
while it is at or before
.Fa t .
.Fn dtfl_probe_done
returns true once the frontier is empty, which happens after every
input feeding the probed stream has closed and the stream has drained.
A program drives a computation by stepping the worker while a probe is
behind the time of interest, or until it is done.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_probe_frontier
returns the frontier as an antichain of
.Fa *n
times of the stream's class, valid until the next worker step.
.Fn dtfl_probe_free
releases the probe.
A probe may be freed after the dataflow that uses it is dropped; the
frontier it shares with the operator is reference counted so either may
outlive the other.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_probe_new
returns a new probe.
.Fn dtfl_stream_probe_with
returns the probed stream.
The predicate functions return a
.Vt bool .
.Fn dtfl_probe_frontier
returns the frontier times and stores their count through
.Fa n .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_probe *p = dtfl_probe_new();
/* inside the build callback: */
dtfl_stream_probe_with(stream, p);

/* step the worker until the probe passes the current input time. */
for (uint64_t round = 0; round < 10; round++) {
	uint64_t next = round + 1;
	dtfl_input_advance_to(in, &next);
	while (dtfl_probe_less_than(p, &next))
		dtfl_worker_step(w);
}
dtfl_input_close(in);
while (!dtfl_probe_done(p))
	dtfl_worker_step(w);
dtfl_probe_free(p);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_input_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt Probe
trait and its
.Vt Handle .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A
.Vt dtfl_probe
is worker-owned, like upstream's
.Vt ProbeHandle ,
which holds an
.Vt Rc<RefCell<MutableAntichain>> :
it belongs to the thread that runs the worker whose stream it probes and
must not be queried from another thread (PLAN section 5).
The operator updates the shared frontier on that thread and the queries
read it on that thread.
A read-only snapshot that another thread may watch is a planned
addition and is not part of this interface.
